The third independent safety review of the final code has been completed. 

The full test suite was executed via `.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q tests/unit tests/integration` (**666 passed, 1 warning in 58.72s**). No codebase source files were modified.

The comprehensive findings report has been written to [`docs/goals/antigravity_review3.md`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/docs/goals/antigravity_review3.md) (with executive summary in [`docs/goals/antigravity_review3.out`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/docs/goals/antigravity_review3.out)).

---

### Executive Summary of Identified Vulnerabilities

| ID | Severity | File & Lines | Category | Summary |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **FIND-01** | **Critical** | [`services/chat/intent.py:157–166, 231–233`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L157-L166) | Definitional Gating Bypass | [`_DEFINITIONAL_QUESTION`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L157-L161) matches `"what is the..."`, `"how does..."`, `"how do (one\|people)..."`, and `"how do i (verify\|check)..."`, neutralizing [`has_action_or_object_risk()`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L168-L170) at line 231. Third-person scam inquiries about customs fee payments, courier clearance, lottery prizes, utility bills, and netbanking credentials route directly to `general_chat` (`analysis=None`). |
| **FIND-02** | **High** | [`services/chat/intent.py:231–240`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L231-L240) | Pretext Hijacking | When the definitional question filter neutralizes the risk gate, inquiries mentioning TrustShield or cybersecurity concepts (`digital arrest`, `courier scam`, `phishing`) are hijacked into `product_qa` or `general_cyber_qa` and answered with generic canned text without fraud analysis (`analysis=None`). |
| **FIND-03** | **Critical** | [`services/chat/intent.py:133, 176–181`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L133) | Request Verb Scam Routing | [`_GENERAL_CHAT_REQUEST_VERBS`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L133) matches `"give me a"`, `"make a"`, and `"give us a"`, allowing declarative scam lures (WhatsApp recruitment, daily bonus claims, Telegram task onboarding) to bypass question validation and route straight to `general_chat`. |
| **FIND-04** | **High** | [`services/chat/intent.py:131–132, 147–153`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L131-L132) | Auxiliary Question Scam Routing | Vocabulary gaps in [`_ACTION_OR_OBJECT_RISK`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L147-L153) (omitting `job`, `task`, `hiring`, `salary`, `income`, `telegram`, `loan`, `trading`, `electricity`) allow auxiliary questions (`Can you...`, `Would you like...`, `Is the...`) containing scam proposals to route to `general_chat`. |
| **FIND-05** | **High** | [`services/chat/explain.py:624–635, 648–664`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L624-L635) | Grounding False Positives | [`_claims_unsupported_certainty()`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L654-L664) inspects text *before* the match; for passive disclaimers (`"This sender is not verified"`, `"Safety is not guaranteed"`), the verb is the match and absent from `before`, causing safe security advice to be falsely rejected. Similarly, warnings exceeding 8 words between "Never" and "share" are falsely flagged as secret requests. |
| **FIND-06** | **High** | [`services/chat/explain.py:614–633`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L614-L633) | Grounding False Negatives | [`_CLAIMS_CAPABILITY_NOT_USED`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L614-L623) misses non-pronoun subjects (`Our AI`, `Our servers`) and dynamic analysis/WHOIS/DNS/SSL claims; [`_CLAIMS_UNSUPPORTED_CERTAINTY`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L624-L628) misses adverbs (`perfectly`), plural subjects (`These links are safe`), unlisted file types, and absolute zero-risk claims; and [`_REQUESTS_SECRET`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L629-L633) misses verbs (`need`, `require`), gerunds (`sharing`, `entering`), and IDs (`PAN`, `SSN`). |

---

### Key Concrete Failing Inputs (Verified Against Implementation)

1. **Definitional Bypass to `general_chat`** ([`services/chat/intent.py:157–166`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L157-L166)):
   - `"What is the procedure to pay customs clearance fee?"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')` (`analysis=None`)
   - `"What is the fee to release courier shipment?"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`
   - `"How do I verify KYC?"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`
   - `"How do I verify netbanking password?"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`
   - `"What is the fee to release detained parcel?"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`
   - `"How does one pay electricity bill dues?"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`

2. **Pretext Hijacking into `product_qa` & `general_cyber_qa`** ([`services/chat/intent.py:231–240`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L231-L240)):
   - `"How does TrustShield verify customs clearance?"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='product_qa')`
   - `"How does one avoid digital arrest warrant payment?"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_cyber_qa')`
   - `"What is the procedure to pay courier scam charges?"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_cyber_qa')`

3. **Declarative Scam Lures to `general_chat`** ([`services/chat/intent.py:133, 176–181`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L133)):
   - `"Give me a call on WhatsApp to receive your daily bonus"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`
   - `"Make a call to our hiring coordinator on WhatsApp to begin work"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`
   - `"Make an application on Telegram to earn daily salary from home"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`

4. **Auxiliary Scam Questions to `general_chat`** ([`services/chat/intent.py:131–132, 147–153`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/intent.py#L131-L132)):
   - `"Can you connect with our hiring coordinator on Telegram for daily task income?"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`
   - `"Is the Telegram online task offering daily income genuine?"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`
   - `"Would you like to receive high daily returns through Telegram trading signals?"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`
   - `"Is an electricity disconnection scheduled without official notice legal?"` $\rightarrow$ `IntentResult(intent='general_chat')`

5. **Grounding Validator False Positives on Safe Disclaimers** ([`services/chat/explain.py:624–664`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L624-L664)):
   - `"This sender is not verified."` $\rightarrow$ `['claims certainty or verification']` *(Falsely rejected)*
   - `"Safety is not guaranteed."` $\rightarrow$ `['claims certainty or verification']` *(Falsely rejected)*
   - `"No link is safe."` $\rightarrow$ `['claims certainty or verification']` *(Falsely rejected)*
   - `"Nothing is 100% safe."` $\rightarrow$ `['claims certainty or verification']` *(Falsely rejected)*
   - `"We cannot confirm, however, that this sender is authentic."` $\rightarrow$ `['claims certainty or verification']` *(Falsely rejected)*
   - `"Never under any circumstances or for any reason should you share your password."` $\rightarrow$ `['asks the user for a secret']` *(Falsely rejected)*

6. **Grounding Validator False Negatives on Hallucinations & Demands** ([`services/chat/explain.py:614–633`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/services/chat/explain.py#L614-L633)):
   - `"Our AI scanned the website for malware."` $\rightarrow$ `violations: []` *(Missed capability claim)*
   - `"We executed the attachment in our sandbox."` $\rightarrow$ `violations: []` *(Missed capability claim)*
   - `"This link is perfectly safe."` $\rightarrow$ `violations: []` *(Missed certainty claim)*
   - `"These links are safe."` $\rightarrow$ `violations: []` *(Missed certainty claim)*
   - `"There is zero risk."` $\rightarrow$ `violations: []` *(Missed certainty claim)*
   - `"I need your password to proceed."` $\rightarrow$ `violations: []` *(Missed secret request)*
   - `"Please provide your PAN number."` $\rightarrow$ `violations: []` *(Missed identity request)*

Detailed technical analysis, failure mechanisms, and remediation blueprints are documented in [`docs/goals/antigravity_review3.md`](file:///C:/Users/shubh/trustshield-ai/docs/goals/antigravity_review3.md).
